{"id": "cpa-resilient-back-office", "title": "A City grantee's staff work for a company its sister groups own", "seconds": 172.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "e6707dfbeda36b5f", "words": 464, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[12]"], "text": "The Chinese Progressive Association is a San Francisco charity.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.56, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "a San Francisco charity the City funds", "chip": "$1.21 million in fiscal 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.55, 1.02, 2.01, 2.18, 2.25, 2.46, 2.94]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[12]"], "text": "The City paid it 1.21 million dollars in fiscal 2025.", "t0": 3.68, "t1": 7.94, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "a San Francisco charity the City funds", "chip": "$1.21 million in fiscal 2025"}, "emph": ["1.21 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.42, 0.66, 0.78, 1.01, 1.3, 1.6, 1.8, 2.14, 2.79, 2.97, 3.34, 3.59]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]"], "text": "In 2020, it reported 233 employees.", "t0": 8.06, "t1": 12.32, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Its own employees", "sub": "233 in 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 1.11, 1.28, 1.67, 1.96, 2.29, 2.81]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]"], "text": "For 2024, how many?", "t0": 12.32, "t1": 15.59, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Its own employees", "sub": "233 in 2020"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.46, 1.85, 2.08]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "None.", "t0": 15.59, "t1": 16.17, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "0", "label": "employees reported for 2024", "sub": "Chinese Progressive Association, Form 990"}, "emph": ["None"], "wt": [0.04]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 16.69, "t1": 18.35, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.4, 0.99, 1.17, 1.24]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "That’s because its workers are employed by a company, Resilient Strategies.", "t0": 18.47, "t1": 23.39, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "the charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "employer of record"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "The staff", "sub": "who do its work"}], "kicker": "Who employs the staff"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.9, 1.13, 1.46, 1.58, 2.33, 2.55, 2.63, 3.63, 4.23]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "The return calls it the employer of record.", "t0": 23.51, "t1": 25.49, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "the charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "employer of record"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "The staff", "sub": "who do its work"}], "kicker": "Who employs the staff"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.5, 0.76, 0.88, 1.0, 1.49, 1.61]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "So who owns Resilient? Half is reported by the Center for Empowered Politics, a political nonprofit.", "t0": 25.71, "t1": 31.4, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Center for Empowered Politics", "50%"], "b": ["CEP Education Fund", "50%"], "mid": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["political"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.36, 0.66, 1.76, 2.04, 2.15, 2.51, 2.62, 2.72, 2.96, 3.1, 3.58, 4.52, 4.64, 5.05]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "The other half, by its charity arm, the CEP Education Fund.", "t0": 31.52, "t1": 35.49, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Center for Empowered Politics", "50%"], "b": ["CEP Education Fund", "50%"], "mid": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.41, 0.98, 1.15, 1.29, 1.64, 2.17, 2.31, 3.15, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Both call Resilient a related organization.", "t0": 35.61, "t1": 37.79, "shot": "b7a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "a related organization, on both returns"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.61, 1.06, 1.15, 1.47]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[2]"], "text": "CPA’s return, from the same preparer, calls it unrelated.", "t0": 37.91, "t1": 41.27, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Resilient Strategies, an unrelated organization"}, "emph": ["unrelated"], "wt": [0.0, 0.64, 1.12, 1.28, 1.39, 1.71, 2.51, 2.77, 2.85]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[5]"], "text": "Yet CPA’s executive director is the Education Fund’s principal officer.", "t0": 41.39, "t1": 45.47, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "CPA’s executive director", "sub": "the Education Fund’s principal officer"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "CPA’s chief financial officer, 2023", "sub": "the Education Fund’s treasurer"}, {"art": "money", "name": "CEP Education Fund", "sub": "principal officer; treasurer"}], "kicker": "The same people"}, "emph": ["executive director"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.92, 1.34, 2.11, 2.28, 2.39, 2.87, 3.23, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[5]"], "text": "CPA’s 2023 finance chief is its treasurer.", "t0": 45.59, "t1": 48.36, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "CPA’s executive director", "sub": "the Education Fund’s principal officer"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "CPA’s chief financial officer, 2023", "sub": "the Education Fund’s treasurer"}, {"art": "money", "name": "CEP Education Fund", "sub": "principal officer; treasurer"}], "kicker": "The same people"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.69, 0.95, 1.41, 1.8, 2.05, 2.16, 2.33]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[13]"], "text": "And Resilient’s own State filings name that same person as its sole manager.", "t0": 48.48, "t1": 52.62, "shot": "b8a", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ir4a", "kicker": "California Secretary of State · 201928210153", "text": "Resilient Strategies LLC: sole manager and agent: the person listed as CPA’s chief financial officer (2023); principal office 1212 Broadway Suite 700, Oakland", "mark": "sole manager"}, "emph": ["sole manager"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.63, 0.88, 1.19, 1.62, 1.83, 1.99, 2.24, 3.06, 3.26, 3.37, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[14]"], "text": "CPA even gives the charity registry Resilient’s Oakland office as its own address.", "t0": 52.74, "t1": 56.86, "shot": "b8a", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ir4a", "kicker": "California Secretary of State · 201928210153", "text": "Resilient Strategies LLC: sole manager and agent: the person listed as CPA’s chief financial officer (2023); principal office 1212 Broadway Suite 700, Oakland", "mark": "sole manager"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.8, 1.04, 1.13, 1.47, 1.88, 2.45, 2.79, 3.13, 3.26, 3.41, 3.56]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[17]"], "text": "Its 2023 registry report answers no to government funding;", "t0": 56.98, "t1": 60.86, "shot": "b8c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2,056,418", "label": "paid by the City in fiscal 2023", "sub": "the 2023 registry report answers 'No' to government funding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.52, 0.95, 1.36, 1.78, 2.25, 2.65, 2.8, 3.13]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[17]"], "text": "the City paid it 2,056,418 dollars that year.", "t0": 60.86, "t1": 64.4, "shot": "b8c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2,056,418", "label": "paid by the City in fiscal 2023", "sub": "the 2023 registry report answers 'No' to government funding"}, "emph": ["2,056,418"], "wt": [0.04, 0.17, 0.43, 0.63, 0.72, 1.0, 1.41, 1.77, 2.05, 2.38, 3.01, 3.25]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Is “unrelated” wrong? It turns on an IRS test of control.", "t0": 64.52, "t1": 68.41, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The IRS control test", "sub": "do one group’s people hold a majority of the other’s board?"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 1.12, 1.91, 2.05, 2.38, 2.47, 2.58, 3.05, 3.31, 3.39]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "The filings don’t say enough to tell.", "t0": 68.53, "t1": 70.32, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The IRS control test", "sub": "do one group’s people hold a majority of the other’s board?"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.64, 0.86, 1.06, 1.29, 1.41]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "innocent[5]"], "text": "Its own audit files them under “related party”, yet says none controls another.", "t0": 70.44, "t1": 74.97, "shot": "b9x", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“Each organization maintains a unique board with no overlap.”"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.37, 0.68, 1.02, 1.17, 1.33, 1.75, 2.62, 2.87, 3.48, 3.74, 4.17]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "Then the price. What did CPA pay Resilient in 2024? Its return gives three answers.", "t0": 75.19, "t1": 81.58, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "What CPA paid Resilient in 2024, by its own return", "rows": [["Contractor table", "$18,279,136"], ["Schedule O", "$11,935,499"], ["Expenses, line 11a", "$11,404,687"]]}, "emph": ["three answers"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.27, 1.71, 1.87, 1.99, 2.46, 2.66, 3.14, 3.25, 3.51, 4.65, 4.88, 5.35, 5.59, 5.85]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]"], "text": "18,279,136 dollars.", "t0": 81.7, "t1": 83.68, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "What CPA paid Resilient in 2024, by its own return", "rows": [["Contractor table", "$18,279,136"], ["Schedule O", "$11,935,499"], ["Expenses, line 11a", "$11,404,687"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.61, 0.86, 1.13, 1.49]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]"], "text": "11,935,499.", "t0": 83.8, "t1": 85.42, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "What CPA paid Resilient in 2024, by its own return", "rows": [["Contractor table", "$18,279,136"], ["Schedule O", "$11,935,499"], ["Expenses, line 11a", "$11,404,687"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.55, 0.82, 1.17]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]"], "text": "And 11,404,687.", "t0": 85.54, "t1": 87.33, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "What CPA paid Resilient in 2024, by its own return", "rows": [["Contractor table", "$18,279,136"], ["Schedule O", "$11,935,499"], ["Expenses, line 11a", "$11,404,687"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.41, 0.78, 1.07, 1.32]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]", "established[18]"], "text": "Its 2024 audit backs only one: 11,935,499 dollars.", "t0": 87.45, "t1": 92.12, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The audit backs one figure", "sub": "managed services: $11,935,499"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.5, 1.02, 1.32, 1.59, 1.85, 2.6, 2.9, 3.26, 3.54, 3.85, 4.19]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[18]", "story[2]"], "text": "It also gives Resilient’s fee: 10% of spending, and 15% of government-grant spending.", "t0": 92.24, "t1": 98.41, "shot": "b12x", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“an administrative service fee equal to 10% of gross expenses and 15% of Government grant expenses”"}, "emph": ["15%"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.51, 0.86, 1.47, 2.46, 2.72, 3.03, 3.12, 3.95, 4.15, 4.63, 4.97, 5.06, 5.73]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]"], "text": "Campaigns pay Resilient too:", "t0": 98.63, "t1": 101.0, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "$333,814", "label": "paid to Resilient Strategies by San Francisco committees since 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.67, 0.88, 1.44]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]"], "text": "about 333,814 dollars from San Francisco committees.", "t0": 101.0, "t1": 106.63, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "$333,814", "label": "paid to Resilient Strategies by San Francisco committees since 2020"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.37, 0.62, 0.91, 1.42, 2.21, 2.44, 2.95, 3.51, 4.26, 4.46, 4.68, 5.15]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Most came from Tenants and Families United PAC, sponsored by the Center for Empowered Politics.", "t0": 106.75, "t1": 111.78, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Voter Guide Design and Distribution, Aaron Peskin, Support"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.64, 0.82, 1.15, 1.29, 1.67, 2.03, 2.88, 3.41, 3.52, 3.63, 3.87, 4.0, 4.42]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "One entry: a voter guide supporting Aaron Peskin.", "t0": 111.9, "t1": 114.78, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Voter Guide Design and Distribution, Aaron Peskin, Support"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.97, 1.09, 1.39, 1.71, 2.17, 2.4]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[3]", "established[8]"], "text": "Candidates paid that political nonprofit directly.", "t0": 114.9, "t1": 117.38, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Candidate committees paid the Center for Empowered Politics", "rows": [["Chyanne Chen, 2024", "$35,706"], ["Gordon Mar, 2022", "$30,236"], ["Connie Chan, 2024", "$15,669.46"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.83, 0.99, 1.4, 1.96]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[3]", "established[8]"], "text": "Chyanne Chen’s 2024 campaign:", "t0": 117.5, "t1": 120.39, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Candidate committees paid the Center for Empowered Politics", "rows": [["Chyanne Chen, 2024", "$35,706"], ["Gordon Mar, 2022", "$30,236"], ["Connie Chan, 2024", "$15,669.46"]]}, "emph": ["Chyanne Chen"], "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 0.95, 1.21, 1.67]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[3]", "established[8]"], "text": "35,706 dollars, for staffing.", "t0": 120.39, "t1": 124.93, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Candidate committees paid the Center for Empowered Politics", "rows": [["Chyanne Chen, 2024", "$35,706"], ["Gordon Mar, 2022", "$30,236"], ["Connie Chan, 2024", "$15,669.46"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.65, 1.61, 2.04, 2.51, 3.06, 3.93, 4.09]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[9]"], "text": "And the charity? It gave 49,000 dollars to a ballot committee at its own suite.", "t0": 125.15, "t1": 130.53, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Force for Change ballot committee", "kicker": "CPA’s own campaign spending", "sub": "September 24, 2024; listed at CPA’s own suite", "chip": "$49,000"}, "emph": ["49,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.22, 1.47, 1.64, 1.92, 2.51, 3.0, 3.36, 3.47, 3.56, 3.86, 4.37, 4.54, 4.7, 4.97]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "In July 2026, it paid Resilient for staff time on a ballot measure.", "t0": 130.65, "t1": 134.32, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City grants", "sub": "to CPA"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Charity money", "sub": "CPA and the Education Fund"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Campaign money", "sub": "committees and candidates"}], "kicker": "One payroll company"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.51, 0.78, 1.4, 1.52, 1.79, 2.27, 2.41, 2.71, 2.92, 3.0, 3.06, 3.34]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "So City grants, charity money and campaign money all pay one company.", "t0": 134.44, "t1": 137.83, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City grants", "sub": "to CPA"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Charity money", "sub": "CPA and the Education Fund"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Campaign money", "sub": "committees and candidates"}], "kicker": "One payroll company"}, "emph": ["one company"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.46, 0.83, 1.19, 1.39, 1.48, 1.94, 2.19, 2.5, 2.73, 2.93]}, {"scene": "grants", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "One grantee was the Center for Empowered Politics Education Fund.", "t0": 138.05, "t1": 141.2, "shot": "returns0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Annual grant disclosures", "source": "cycle202313189349319436", "text": "Schedule I", "mark": "Schedule I"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.75, 0.93, 1.03, 1.28, 1.41, 1.89, 2.35, 2.83]}, {"scene": "grants", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "In 2022, each reported a grant to another of the three organizations.", "t0": 141.32, "t1": 145.27, "shot": "returns1", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Schedule I · separate grants", "heading": "2022 grant disclosures", "source": "cycle202313189349319436", "rows": [{"icon": "transfer", "label": "CPA → Education Fund", "value": "$15,000"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Education Fund → Tides Center", "value": "$50,000"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Tides Center → CPA", "value": "$75,000"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 1.22, 1.49, 1.91, 1.97, 2.3, 2.45, 2.78, 2.84, 2.93, 3.15]}, {"scene": "grants", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "The three connections appear again in 2023, for different amounts.", "t0": 145.39, "t1": 149.36, "shot": "returns2", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Schedule I · separate grants", "heading": "2023 grant disclosures", "source": "cycle202423199349319082", "rows": [{"icon": "transfer", "label": "CPA → Education Fund", "value": "$116,000"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Education Fund → Tides Center", "value": "$10,000"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Tides Center → CPA", "value": "$384,000"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 0.91, 1.17, 1.52, 1.63, 1.92, 3.04, 3.19, 3.47]}, {"scene": "grants", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "The grants had different purposes. The returns provide no dates for individual payments.", "t0": 149.48, "t1": 154.43, "shot": "returns3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Annual disclosures", "source": "cycle202412739349300301", "text": "Different grants · individual payment dates unavailable", "mark": "Different grants"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.73, 1.07, 2.12, 2.28, 2.8, 3.21, 3.46, 3.84, 4.0, 4.47]}, {"scene": "grants", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "The project ledgers would show whether the same money moved through the organizations.", "t0": 154.55, "t1": 158.22, "shot": "returns4", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Which projects were funded", "Whether the same money moved"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.47, 0.83, 0.98, 1.19, 1.44, 1.56, 1.9, 2.19, 2.5, 2.72, 2.81]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]"], "text": "No record shows City money paying for campaign work.", "t0": 158.44, "t1": 160.86, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That City grant money paid for campaign work", "Why the return gives two other figures"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.54, 0.84, 1.08, 1.32, 1.59, 1.72, 2.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? CPA’s agreement with Resilient, and the timesheets behind its City grants.", "t0": 160.98, "t1": 165.89, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "CPA’s agreement with Resilient, and how shared staff are split"}, {"who": "", "what": "Invoices and timesheets behind the City grants"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.35, 0.66, 1.21, 1.85, 2.23, 2.39, 2.97, 3.14, 3.23, 3.82, 4.11, 4.23, 4.46]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has tested CPA’s “unrelated” answer.", "t0": 166.01, "t1": 169.26, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.64, 0.82, 1.16, 2.05, 2.84]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 169.38, "t1": 171.48, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.4, 0.47, 1.18, 1.36, 1.45]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The charity", "lead1": "Lead 1 · related or unrelated", "lead2": "Lead 2 · three amounts", "lead3": "Lead 3 · campaign money", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the charity’s own", "close": "Where it stands", "grants": "Grants between the organizations"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "contrast"}